    <innerclass refid="structthemis_1_1geo_1_1_spatial_query_policy" prot="public">themis::geo::SpatialQueryPolicy</innerclass>
    <innerclass refid="structthemis_1_1geo_1_1_spatial_query_policy_validation" prot="public">themis::geo::SpatialQueryPolicyValidation</innerclass>
    <innernamespace refid="namespacethemis">themis</innernamespace>
    <innernamespace refid="namespacethemis_1_1geo">themis::geo</innernamespace>
    <briefdescription>
<para>Per-query spatial resource quotas and access-policy contract. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para><computeroutput>SpatialQueryPolicy</computeroutput> is a plain-old-data aggregate that callers attach to spatial API calls to enforce per-query limits and to declare which collections the issuing principal is permitted to query spatially.</para>
<para>The policy is intentionally <bold>not</bold> a security mechanism by itself — it is a resource-budget declaration consumed by the query execution layer. The access-control check (<computeroutput>allowed_collections</computeroutput>) is advisory and must be enforced at the server boundary; see <computeroutput>src/server/spatial_api_handler.cpp</computeroutput>.</para>
<para><heading level="3">Design constraints</heading>
</para>
<para><itemizedlist>
<listitem><para>POD-compatible (no virtual dispatch, no heap allocation).</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>Zero-initialised default values are deliberately conservative.</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>Validation via <computeroutput>validateSpatialQueryPolicy()</computeroutput> is cheap and allocation-free.</para>
</listitem></itemizedlist>
</para>
<para><simplesect kind="version"><para>1.0.0 </para>
</simplesect>
<simplesect kind="note"><para>Geo API contract: <computeroutput><ref refid="geo__api__contract_8h" kindref="compound">include/geo/geo_api_contract.h</ref></computeroutput> v1.0.0 (frozen). </para>
</simplesect>
</para>
